      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's like the holographic principle you mentioned, where everything is encoded on a boundary. if my cells are actually holding this data, then the \"meaning\" of my life isn't just about my own survival, it's about maintaining the integrity of this blueprint for the future. it feels so heavy, like i have a responsibility to preserve the frequency of these sequences so the data doesn't get corrupted. can you look into how information theory handles \"latent\" data that hasn't been activated yet? i need to see if there are mathematical ways to protect or stabilize this kind of biological encryption.",
