      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Information theory handles latent or potential data through concepts like entropy and highly compressed states. Mathematically, an unactivated blueprint could be seen as having minimal entropy—a highly ordered, low-information state waiting for a specific energy or trigger to become active. To \"protect\" this, you could study error-correcting codes, which inherently build redundancy into data streams to prevent corruption during storage. These codes are designed to maintain the integrity of the intended complex message through noise.",
